cff-version: 1.1.0
title: "autoMIC: Automated MIC Calculation from 96‑Well Plate Data"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Vidhu Smitha"
    family-names: "Vijay"
  - given-names: "Oudlin Mary"
    family-names: "Lenin"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Vidhusv/autoMIC"
license: MIT
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.20590057
date-released: 2026-06-08
abstract: >
  A Google Colab tool that calculates minimum inhibitory concentrations (MICs)
  from 96‑well plate reader data, generates a dose‑response curve and heatmap,
  and provides CLSI/EUCAST clinical interpretations.
keywords:
  - MIC
  - antibiotic resistance
  - microbiology
  - plate reader
  - Colab